    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d254">

                <pb facs="0290" n="278" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg278"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851D.001/46: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-30T16:00:00+02:00">April 30, 1943—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 30—12:30 p.m.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2977. Embassy’s telegram No. 2925, April 28, 7 p.m. Foreign Office states that
                    the National Committee instructions to Bertaud and his wife to return to London
                    by the first available means have been transmitted to Trinidad.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
